From: Octavo (local foliate-js patch set)
Subject: [PATCH 0003] fixed-layout: report going to the other page of a spread

Going to a page of the spread already open (a contents entry, a bookmark, a
saved place) shows that page when one page shows at a time, but leaves #side
on the old one and reports nothing. So the host's position stays on the old
page, and the next resize puts the old page back.

Keeps #side and reports the location, as going to any other spread does.

Checked on the Duo simulator (docs/notes/fixed-layout.md, "Going to a page in
the same spread"): folded on page 6, going to page 7 reported nothing without
this patch and a resize went back to page 6; with it, page 7 was reported and
stayed.

Applies on top of 0002. Apply from the repo root:
  git apply --directory=ReaderWeb/foliate-js ReaderWeb/foliate-js/patches/0003-fixed-layout-same-spread.patch
---
diff --git a/fixed-layout.js b/fixed-layout.js
index c582aba..2f87edd 100644
--- a/fixed-layout.js
+++ b/fixed-layout.js
@@ -265,7 +265,9 @@ export class FixedLayout extends HTMLElement {
     async goToSpread(index, side, reason) {
         if (index < 0 || index > this.#spreads.length - 1) return
         if (index === this.#index) {
+            this.#side = side
             this.#render(side)
+            this.#reportLocation(reason)
             return
         }
         this.#index = index
